{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Discovered while fixing bug regardable-superduper-whiteeye (dca1-f641-caeb-4df4). That ticket\nfixed ONE test; this one covers the rest of the class, which was surveyed but deliberately left\nout of that change to keep its scope honest.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nA test fixture creates a bare git repository with a raw `git init --bare` and pushes into it. At\ngit's defaults a bare repository's `receive-pack` runs `run_auto_maintenance()` after every push,\nspawning `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach` — a background process that OUTLIVES the\npush. `subprocess.run([... \"push\" ...], check=True)` returning is therefore NOT a happens-before\nedge for that repository's object database.\n\nIf the test then COPIES or byte-walks that directory, it races a concurrent repack: entries vanish\nmid-walk and the copy raises. Measured signatures include a vanished `objects/maintenance.lock`\n(what CI caught) and whole loose-object fanout directories (`objects/2c`, `objects/2d`, ...) being\npruned as maintenance packs them.\n\nrebar pins `gc.autoDetach=false` / `maintenance.autoDetach=false` on every store it OWNS\n(`_commands/_init_ensures.py`'s gc-config ensure unit; bug 88eb, ADR 0051). A bare remote built by\na test fixture is owned by no rebar code, so it runs at git's defaults. That asymmetry is the gap.\n\n## Approach\n\nThe remedy is settled and measured — pin three keys on the bare repo immediately after creating\nit, before anything is pushed:\n\n    gc.autoDetach=false\n    maintenance.autoDetach=false\n    receive.autogc=false\n\nMeasured postures (all with `receive-pack` confirmed present in a `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` trace): git\ndefaults -> 1 detached maintenance child; autoDetach pins only -> 1 foreground child; all three\npins -> 0 children. Structural, not probabilistic.\n\nThis change does three things:\n\n1. **Extract one shared definition.** A new `tests/_git_upkeep.py` owns the pins\n   (`BARE_REMOTE_UPKEEP_PINS`), the constructor that applies them (`init_bare_remote`), and the\n   `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` trace reader that proves their effect (`maintenance_children`,\n   `assert_no_detached_upkeep`). It follows the established small single-purpose\n   `tests/_*.py` helper convention (`_git_counts.py`, `_engine_path.py`, `_subprocess_env.py`).\n   `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py` and\n   `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` — which today hold byte-identical copies of the\n   same three keys under two different names — are repointed at it, ending the drift.\n\n2. **Fix the two HIGH-risk sites** by routing their bare-repo creation through that helper.\n\n3. **Make the class un-reintroducible at the amplifier.** `clone_topology_template`\n   (`tests/_topology_template.py`) is the only mechanism in `tests/` that copies a whole topology\n   containing a bare remote — it does `shutil.copytree(...)` plus two full-tree `rglob(\"*\")` +\n   `read_bytes()` passes. It gains a precondition that REFUSES a template containing a bare\n   repository that is not pinned, naming the unpinned path and the missing keys. A future fixture\n   that reintroduces the pattern then fails loudly and deterministically at setup instead of\n   flaking under a race.\n\nExplicitly NOT acceptable as fixes, for the reasons recorded on dca1: retrying the copy, sleeping\nbefore it, or excluding `*.lock` from the walk. The `*.lock` filter in particular is measurably\ninsufficient — the repack limb prunes whole fanout directories, not just lock files.\n\n## The two HIGH-risk sites (push, then the tree containing the bare repo is copied)\n\n1. `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py` — `_git(remote, \"init\", \"-q\", \"--bare\")` in\n   `_build_backup_fixture`; pushes immediately after (`push --all`, `push --tags`); the topology is\n   copied via `clone_topology_template` once per test in the module. No pins anywhere in the file.\n2. `tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py` — `git init -q --bare` in\n   `_build_repo_with_origin`; `rebar.init_repo(...)` pushes under the default\n   `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always`; copied via `clone_topology_template`. No pins.\n\n## The MEDIUM sites: bounded by the amplifier, not swept\n\nThe survey counted ~35 further sites that push into an unpinned bare repo. They are NOT swept in\nthis change, and the reason is a measured exposure predicate rather than a judgement call: a site\nis exposed only when the bare remote lives inside a tree that is later copied or byte-walked, and\n`clone_topology_template` is the only thing in `tests/` that does that to a whole topology. It has\nseven callers; two are the HIGH sites above, one is the already-pinned\n`test_concurrency_regression.py`, one is the module itself, and the remaining three\n(`tests/interfaces/_store_template.py`, `tests/interfaces/queries/test_list_filters.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_secret_screen_e7a9.py`) create no bare repository at all. Every other site pushes\ninto a bare repo that nothing ever copies, so there is no walk to race.\n\nSweeping three config keys across ~35 unaffected files would be a large unreviewable diff whose\nbulk is unnecessary. Step 3 replaces that sweep with an enforced precondition: the moment any of\nthose sites acquires a copy step, the guard converts it from a latent flake into a deterministic\nsetup failure that names the fix. The exposed set is therefore closed by construction rather than\nby an enumeration that decays.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/_git_upkeep.py` (new) — the single definition of the pins, the bare-remote constructor,\n  and the trace-based proof helpers.\n- `tests/_topology_template.py` — add the unpinned-bare-repo precondition to\n  `clone_topology_template`.\n- `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py` — delete its local copy of the pins, consume\n  the shared helper.\n- `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` — delete its local copy of the pins and its local\n  trace reader, consume the shared helper.\n- `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py` — build the bare remote through the helper;\n  add the no-detached-upkeep guard.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py` — build the bare remote through the helper;\n  add the no-detached-upkeep guard.\n- `tests/unit/test_topology_template_upkeep_guard.py` (new) — cover the amplifier precondition\n  both ways.\n\nThis change is stacked on Gerrit 1952 (the dca1 fix), which is `Verified +1` / `LLM-Review +1` but\nnot yet submitted; it introduces the second copy of the pins that step 1 collapses.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: a push into each newly-pinned remote leaves no detached background upkeep — asserted\n  from git's own `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` process trace, behind a `receive-pack` positive control so the\n  assertion cannot pass against an empty trace.\n- Failure path: `clone_topology_template` raises `AssertionError` naming the unpinned bare\n  repository and the missing keys when handed a template containing one, and returns normally for\n  the same template once pinned.\n- Discrimination: for every site changed, seed the defect its test guards, observe RED on the\n  expected assertion, revert, observe GREEN; and separately empty the pins and observe the trace\n  guard fire.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/` contains exactly one definition of the bare-remote upkeep pins; checked by\n      `grep -rn \"receive.autogc\" tests/` finding a single assignment site, in `tests/_git_upkeep.py`.\n- [ ] `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py` and\n      `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` both consume that shared definition rather\n      than their own copy; checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py` creates its bare remote with the pins\n      applied before its first push; checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] `tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py` creates its bare remote with the pins\n      applied before its first push; checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] A push into each newly-pinned remote leaves no detached background upkeep; checked by a test\n      per site that runs the push under `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` and asserts no `git maintenance run`\n      child carries `--detach`, with a `receive-pack` positive control so it cannot pass vacuously.\n- [ ] `clone_topology_template` refuses a template containing an unpinned bare repository, and\n      accepts the same template once pinned; checked by\n      `tests/unit/test_topology_template_upkeep_guard.py` covering both directions.\n- [ ] Each newly-pinned site's guard genuinely discriminates; checked by seeding the defect it\n      guards and observing RED with the expected assertion, then reverting and observing GREEN.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py\n      tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py\n      tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py tests/unit/test_topology_template_upkeep_guard.py -q`\n      is green; checked by that command.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n      (requiring `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`) all pass; checked by running each.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787209873312651001,"uuid":"4b047e27-6ea0-433c-8408-0a36525731b3"}